{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I am reckoned</b> — On account of my manifold poverty and the alteration of my form. Ben Balaam said: it is like כי איל תאר, as in עם גבר תמים. In my opinion: it is a noun in the pattern of ביום קרב, and the word לו is missing, in abbreviated fashion, 'no strength has he,' and similar is ולאין אונים לו, for the meaning is 'for he has no strength.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 88, :notes {0 "Resolved the epithet בן בלעם (lit. 'son of Balaam') as a personal name; identity of this figure is uncertain. The phrase דרך קצרה אין כח לו is textually difficult and translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:19.192709270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}